From: rawdanger-recomp <rawdanger-recomp@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 14:45:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 0023-game-colour-filter-one-pass

Raw Danger's colour filter (its brightness tint and depth haze: after the bloom, the frame walked one 64 x 32 page at a time,
about 2,800 small draws a frame each reading what the one before wrote) recognised in the GS stream and done in one pass:
the walk's draws are left out, their palettes and blend weights noted as they pass, and one formula runs over the frame
(software renderer: rdfilter::finish in gs.cpp; GPU: the game_filter pass in gs.wgsl, every sample at any internal
resolution). Checked against the game's own draws: the same picture to the last bit (software renderer, and the GPU at 1x
and 2x). GPU runs a frame 2,065 -> 105; 300 frames at 1x 78 s -> 37.6 s (35.6 s with the filter off). PS2_GAME_FILTER_PASS=1.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
